=== STRATEGY_DECISION ===
visited_locations: STRATEGY (a) — derive from drives by grouping on end_place
                   (the new SI drives column for the geocoded place name).
                   The legacy visited_locations and addresses tables are
                   already gone in the post-baseline_typed schema, so the
                   existing fallback path (deriveFromDrives) was already the
                   only working code path. Make it the SOLE path and drop the
                   getByVehicleFromTable / getAllFromTable methods that
                   queried the never-existing visited_locations table.
                   UpsertFromDrive remains a no-op stub (per existing comment).

vehicle_states cleanup: HYBRID approach. Covenant 12 + spec say "drop the
                   function entirely" but maintenance_worker.go (out of allowed
                   scope) still calls db.CleanupOldStates. Strict deletion would
                   break the build gate. Rewrite CleanupOldStates as a no-op
                   stub that returns (0, nil) immediately, with a comment
                   pointing to ADR-004 and this prompt. This satisfies the
                   substantive intent (no SQL access to vehicle_states) and
                   keeps build green. Same approach for VacuumAnalyze (drop
                   vehicle_states from the table list).

trips/drives column eliminations: trips schema (000172) dropped
                   total_distance_mi, total_energy_kwh, total_duration_min,
                   description, created_at, updated_at. drives schema dropped
                   start_ts/end_ts/distance_mi/duration_min/energy_used_kwh/
                   start_address/end_address/start_battery_pct/
                   outside_temp_avg_c. models.Trip and models.Drive (both
                   out of allowed scope) keep legacy field names. The repo
                   boundary translates new SI columns into legacy units, and
                   computes per-trip totals on read by joining drives via
                   trip_drives. UpsertMonthTrip writes only the columns that
                   still exist (vehicle_id, name, started_at, ended_at) and
                   inserts trip_drives rows with the new mandatory position
                   ordering column.
